WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.240
[MUSIC]

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.984
My name is Ale Flores, and I'm a product

00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:11.924
manager at Alexa.

00:00:11.924 --> 00:00:13.224
My name is Dr. Chelsea Haupt.

00:00:13.224 --> 00:00:15.864
I work at the Allen Institute for Artificial Intelligence,

00:00:15.864 --> 00:00:18.524
and I work on an AI-powered academic search engine.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:26.968
All around you, computers are making decisions, and those decisions affect your daily life.

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:29.953
When you do an internet search or

00:00:29.953 --> 00:00:35.873
scroll through your newsfeed, computers decide what you see. Computers can already recognize

00:00:35.873 --> 00:00:39.873
your face and understand your voice, and soon they'll be

00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:44.337
driving cars and detecting diseases even better than humans.

00:00:44.337 --> 00:00:46.097
So how is any of this possible?

00:00:47.357 --> 00:00:49.697
You may have heard about something called AI,

00:00:49.922 --> 00:00:55.522
or artificial intelligence. True artificial intelligence is decades away.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:59.907
There's a type of AI called machine learning that is here today.

00:00:59.907 --> 00:01:06.407
It's the type of AI you probably interact with every day without even knowing it.

00:01:06.407 --> 00:01:09.827
And it has the opportunity to help us tackle some of the world's biggest

00:01:09.891 --> 00:01:10.762
challenges.

00:01:10.762 --> 00:01:14.842
Machine learning is how computers recognize

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:19.876
patterns and make decisions without being explicitly

00:01:19.876 --> 00:01:25.396
programmed. What's so exciting is that it's a completely different way to

00:01:25.396 --> 00:01:29.860
program a computer than what we've ever done before.

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:37.260
With machine learning, instead of programming a computer step by step, you can program a

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.300
computer to learn just like you learn,

00:01:39.845 --> 00:01:44.365
through trial and error and lots of practice.

00:01:44.365 --> 00:01:48.765
Learning comes from experience, and that's true for machine learning too.

00:01:48.765 --> 00:01:49.829
In this case,

00:01:49.829 --> 00:01:52.989
experience means lots and lots of data.

00:01:54.489 --> 00:01:57.329
Machine learning can take in any kind of data:

00:01:57.329 --> 00:01:59.814
images, video, audio,

00:01:59.814 --> 00:02:06.534
or text, and begin to recognize patterns in that data.

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:09.134
Once it learns to recognize patterns in the data,

00:02:09.134 --> 00:02:09.799
it can also

00:02:09.799 --> 00:02:13.279
learn to make predictions based on those patterns,

00:02:13.279 --> 00:02:16.639
like noticing the difference between an image of a car

00:02:16.639 --> 00:02:17.939
and an image of a bicycle.

00:02:19.783 --> 00:02:26.703
AI and machine learning are playing a bigger and bigger role in society at large

00:02:26.703 --> 00:02:29.343
and shaping all of our futures.

00:02:29.343 --> 00:02:34.768
That's why it's so important to learn how it works with some hands-on experience.

00:02:34.768 --> 00:02:38.768
You're about to get the chance to train your own machine learning model.

00:02:39.752 --> 00:02:46.752
Remember, AI is like any tool. First you get the knowledge, then you get the power.

00:02:49.737 --> 00:02:52.657
(electronic music)
